The two project objects originate in a substantial but heterogeneous literature. Nazarenko (2013)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U01 source_ids=P33-S01 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S01}
 supplies the compact genus-two octagon-family and generator context from which the frozen control is drawn. Aigon-Dupuy et al.~(2005)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U02 source_ids=P33-S02 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S02}
 provide peer-reviewed family-level context for genus-two hyperbolic octagons and Fuchsian descriptions. For the target, Aurich et al.~(1991)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U03 source_ids=P33-S05 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S05}
 provide regular-octagon matrices, a length relation, and a periodic-orbit enumeration precedent, while Katz et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U04 source_ids=P33-S08 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S08}
 provide arithmetic-Fuchsian and quaternion-order context for the Bolza surface. Grácio and Sousa Ramos (2010)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U05 source_ids=P33-S09 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S09}
 connect symbolic dynamics and fundamental-group words to genus-two length-spectrum computation. These contributions support objects and candidate-generation contexts; they are not treated as completed P33 owner censuses.

The target is similarly treated through bounded complementary context. Aurich et al.~(1991)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U10 source_ids=P33-S05 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S05}
 provide regular-octagon periodic-orbit and matrix context, and Katz et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U11 source_ids=P33-S08 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S08}
 provide exact arithmetic and quaternion-order context for Bolza. Jenni (1984)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U12 source_ids=P33-S06 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S06}
 remains PLAUSIBLE, page-unpinned, and context-only in the frozen verifier; it is not used here to assert an exact systole theorem or formula. Schmutz (1993)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U13 source_ids=P33-S07 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S07}
 supplies broader extremal and systolic context without independently validating the project replay inequality. Thus object identity, arithmetic characterization, systolic context, and below-cutoff owner closure remain separate evidence surfaces.

Strohmaier and Uski (2013, corrected 2018)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U22 source_ids=P33-S16,P33-S16-CORR anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S16,P33-S16-CORR}
 illustrate a separation among bounded computation, error control, and completeness reasoning for spectral objects on hyperbolic surfaces; their 2018 correction is cited separately, remains confined to its recorded scope, and their determinant endpoint is outside P33. Johansson (2017)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U23 source_ids=P33-S17 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S17}
 presents arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius arithmetic with explicit error radii. Rump (2010)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U24 source_ids=P33-S18 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S18}
 surveys rigorous verification using floating-point computation. These works support proof-bearing enclosure discipline for appropriate numerical predicates, but interval arithmetic does not decide group conjugacy or primitivity.

Correction metadata is now dual-bound at every affected use while locator boundaries remain unchanged. The Takeuchi record retains its correction binding (Takeuchi, 1975)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U27 source_ids=P33-S03,P33-S03-CORR anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S03,P33-S03-CORR}
, and the Strohmaier-Uski record retains its 2018 correction binding (Strohmaier and Uski, 2013, corrected 2018)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U28 source_ids=P33-S16,P33-S16-CORR anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S16,P33-S16-CORR}
. Epstein and Holt (2006)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U29 source_ids=P33-S12 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S12}
 retains pages 287--305. Jenni (1984)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U30 source_ids=P33-S06 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S06}
 remains PLAUSIBLE, page-unpinned, and context-only.

The literature supports the three-package architecture only at component and precedent level. Voight (2009)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U31 source_ids=P33-S10 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S10}
 and Despré et al.~(2023)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U32 source_ids=P33-S11 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S11}
 support different domain or presentation pathways. Epstein and Holt (2006)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U33 source_ids=P33-S12 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S12}
 and Lysenok (1990)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U34 source_ids=P33-S13 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S13}
 support conjugacy and root-decision components. Cherubini et al.~(2022)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U35 source_ids=P33-S14 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S14}
 and Erlandsson and Souto (2024)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U36 source_ids=P33-S15 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S15}
 motivate separate primitive, repetition, reciprocal, and inverse-pair semantics. Strohmaier and Uski (2013, with the separately cited 2018 correction)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U37 source_ids=P33-S16,P33-S16-CORR anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S16,P33-S16-CORR}
, Johansson (2017)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U38 source_ids=P33-S17 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S17}
, and Rump (2010)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U39 source_ids=P33-S18 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S18}
 support rigorous predicate and enclosure discipline. Hoffman et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U40 source_ids=P33-S19 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S19}
 and Hales et al.~(2017)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U41 source_ids=P33-S20 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S20}
 support the broader producer-validator pattern. None supplies the missing P33 implementation or scientific result.

The frozen literature supports genus-two octagon objects, Bolza context, and candidate-generation precedents, but it does not itself identify unique primitive inverse-paired owners. Nazarenko (2013)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U42 source_ids=P33-S01 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S01}
 and Aigon-Dupuy et al.~(2005)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U43 source_ids=P33-S02 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S02}
 bound the control-family context. Aurich et al.~(1991)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U44 source_ids=P33-S05 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S05}
, Katz et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U45 source_ids=P33-S08 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S08}
, and Grácio and Sousa Ramos (2010)
% ARS-CITE use_id=P33-U46 source_ids=P33-S09 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE locator_disposition=EXPLICIT_BOUNDED_UNAVAILABLE
\citep{P33-S09}
 bound complementary target and candidate-generation contexts. No cited source is converted into a project-level full-conjugacy, maximal-root, inverse-pair, or completeness certificate.
